  "caption_final": "Avengers: Doomsday sold more than ₹10 crore of opening-day tickets in India within about 19 hours of bookings opening, trade tracker Sacnilk reports. That is around 1 lakh tickets across PVR, INOX and Cinepolis.\n\nFor scale, Avengers: Endgame took ₹8.27 crore in its first 24 hours of advance sales at the same three chains in 2019, and Spider-Man: No Way Home ₹6.56 crore in 2021. Koimoi also reports Doomsday has passed both.\n\nThe priciest seat reported so far is a 4DX 3D midnight show at Cinepolis in Navi Mumbai: ₹4,200, or about ₹4,300 with booking fees. The film opens in Indian cinemas on Thursday, 17 December, a day before its US release.\n\nWhat's the most you'd pay for a movie ticket?\n\nFull story on idly.news (link in bio).\n\n#AvengersDoomsday #Marvel #MCU #BoxOffice #idlynerd\n\nImage: Marvel Entertainment (official trailer)",
